    "conclusion": "PPFD takes three values (200, 400, 750 umol/m2/s) and is varied inside every experiment. Air and root-zone temperature take four values overall (20, 24, 28, 32 C) but only two inside any one experiment, and the four experiments cover the four quadrants: EXP1 20/24-20/24, EXP2 20/24-28/32, EXP3 28/32-20/24, EXP4 28/32-28/32. So temperature is a gradient with two levels per experiment, confounded with experiment identity, while light is a clean three-level within-experiment gradient. Leave-one-experiment-out cross-validation therefore removes one temperature quadrant at a time and asks the model to place a quadrant it has never seen."
  },
